From b226e0dcfb143f81d58edd51e17d0c1343a52ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:23:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] apps: paper/ink static incoming call page

The incoming call (answer) page of a voice call now matches the paper/ink
ongoing-call page and has no motion.

- Two static buttons for every incoming voice call: AnswerMethodFactory
  returns TwoButtonMethod instead of the swipe puck. Video calls and
  video upgrade requests keep the stock path (swipe puck, or two buttons
  with TalkBack or in multi-window), styling and animations, so the
  camera preview page is unchanged.
- Answer is a solid black circle with a white call icon, Decline a white
  circle with a 1dp ink ring and a black icon (incall_eink_button); both
  show black labels. Pressed/focused states are static: Answer inverts to
  white with a 2dp edge, Decline gets the 2dp edge. Ids, sizes, hit
  areas, content descriptions and callbacks are those of the stock
  two-button layout; TalkBack's touch handler is kept.
- No animators on this page: no contact grid entry animation, no
  scale/fade-out before answering or declining (the call is answered or
  declined at once), hint text shown or hidden at once, no fades of the
  secondary actions, no importance-badge transition.
- White page and window background with dark status/navigation icons,
  like the ongoing-call page (InCallActivity paper/ink window now covers
  the voice answer screen too); the page, avatar and two-button method
  use Theme.InCallScreen.Eink (black text, white letter tiles). The
  avatar has no elevation and the ink outline of the ongoing-call page;
  real photos are not recoloured.
- "Reject with message" and "Answer and end ongoing call" are plain
  outlined text buttons (MainEink.EmptyAction) below the main buttons,
  always clickable and focusable, with the visibility and actions of the
  swipe affordances they replace; those stay gone.
- The reply sheet is the white outlined sheet of the audio route picker
  without dim or window animation, with black rows and static press
  outlines; the custom message dialog uses the main page's MainEink
  dialog theme.

Call handling, Telecom, ringing, proximity, lock screen display and the
ongoing-call page are unchanged.

Change-Id: I2b380f230efcfad888012a5be64c5ce92fe7a7cb

One action per call on the paper/ink page: once Answer, Decline, "Answer
and end ongoing call" or a reply is chosen, further taps are ignored
(answer-and-release sets the accept flag before calling the delegate),
and the reply sheet or dialog cannot open twice. The swipe-worded
call-waiting hints are hidden there; the outlined button names the
action.
